**Roles & editor features:**
- From GET /api/trees we get role per tree. Tree list shows role badge.
- If role editor/creator → "Add person" button opening simple form → POST /api/trees/<id>/persons {fields}. Fields whitelisted unknown exactly; contract says person fields include name, gender, dob, dod at minimum (from partners payload), plus height, weight, address, mail, phone, job, degree, place, other_info (from big modal requirement). I'll send those fields present in the form. Partial update PUT for edit? Not required — nice-to-have only Add person. Keep scope: Add person button + modal form. Must not block read flow.
- Delete tree button for creator? DELETE /api/trees creator-only. Not explicitly required in flow, but role display required. I'll add a subtle delete on the trees list for creators — hmm, scope discipline: "Show role from GET /api/trees; if role is editor or creator show an Add person button..." Only that is required beyond read flow. Adding destructive delete buttons not requested — skip it. Keep smallest correct scope. Maybe skip. Yes skip delete tree UI.

**Error banners + loading states + responsive 360px.**

**API client details:**
- All requests: `fetch(path, {headers, credentials:'same-origin'})`. JSON bodies with Content-Type application/json. Multipart for photo upload — photo upload endpoint exists (POST /api/persons/:pid/photo) but is photo upload UI required? The big modal displays photo. Upload UI isn't in the professor flow. Skip upload UI (editor+ nicety, not required). Actually "nice-to-have, must not block read flow" applied to Add person. Photo upload not mentioned as required UI. Skip.
- Handle non-JSON responses safely; errors are JSON {error:string}.
- 401 handling: global interceptor — if a request 401s while on protected route, redirect to #/login.

**Login page:** combined login/signup. Tabs switching between Sign in / Create account. Signup fields: email, name, password, lang (select: en, hi, ta, bn — kinship terms support these four languages). Default lang en. After success navigate #/trees. Show server error messages (409 duplicate etc.).

**State:** module-level object: `state = { me: null, meLoaded: false }`.

**Router:** parse location.hash: `#/login`, `#/trees`, `#/tree/<id>`, default → redirect based on auth. hashchange listener re-renders into #app root. Guard: protected routes require me loaded; await ensureMe() once.

